{"book":{"id":"book-judgment-days-lyndon-baines-johnson-martin-luther-king-jr-and-the-laws-that-changed-america-nick","slug":"judgment-days-lyndon-baines-johnson-martin-luther-king-jr-and-the-laws-that-changed-america-nick","title":"Judgment Days: Lyndon Baines Johnson, Martin Luther King Jr., and the Laws That Changed America","authors":[{"id":"person-nick-kotz","name":"Nick Kotz"}],"isbn13":["9780618641833"],"subjects":["Race & Ethnicity"],"topics":["Vietnam War","Civil Rights & Racial Justice","Courts & Trials","Democracy & Elections"],"centralFigures":["Lyndon Baines Johnson","Martin Luther King Jr."],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Judgment%20Days%3A%20Lyndon%20Baines%20Johnson%2C%20Martin%20Luther%20King%20Jr.%2C%20and%20the%20Laws%20That%20Changed%20America%20Nick%20Kotz","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=Judgment%20Days%3A%20Lyndon%20Baines%20Johnson%2C%20Martin%20Luther%20King%20Jr.%2C%20and%20the%20Laws%20That%20Changed%20America%20Nick%20Kotz","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=Judgment%20Days%3A%20Lyndon%20Baines%20Johnson%2C%20Martin%20Luther%20King%20Jr.%2C%20and%20the%20Laws%20That%20Changed%20America%20Nick%20Kotz","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=Judgment%20Days%3A%20Lyndon%20Baines%20Johnson%2C%20Martin%20Luther%20King%20Jr.%2C%20and%20the%20Laws%20That%20Changed%20America%20Nick%20Kotz","publisher":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL4987512W"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-rfk-book-award-robert-f-kennedy-human-rights-official-laureate-page-nick-kotz","source-open-library-summary-judgment-days-lyndon-baines-johnson-martin-luther-king-jr-and-the-laws-that-changed-america-nick"],"readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0.114,"accessibilityScore":0.014,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[{"id":"character_driven","score":0.18,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"portrait of\""]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Lyndon Baines Johnson","confidence":0.9},{"name":"Martin Luther King Jr.","confidence":0.88}],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":false,"statement":"","confidence":0},"academicOrientation":{"score":40,"confidence":0.45},"profileConfidence":0.77,"lowerConfidenceCandidates":{"argument":{"statement":"Johnson and Martin Luther King Jr.’s initially hostile relationship, informed by newly available communications, was pivotal in advancing the Civil Rights Act of 1964 and the Voting Rights Act of 1965.","confidence":0.56}},"model":"gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"4224140a32f36e6f45297db385151000f92982c0401d4d4fd796abffe057d7fe","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"summary":"The first comprehensive account of the relationship between President Johnson and Martin Luther King uses FBI wiretaps, Johnson's taped telephone conversations, and previously undisclosed communications between the two to paint a fascinating portrait of this important relationship. Opposites in almost every way, mortally suspicious of each other at first, Lyndon Baines Johnson and Martin Luther King, Jr., were thrust together in the aftermath of John F. Kennedy's assassination. Both men sensed a historic opportunity and began a delicate dance of accommodation that moved them, and the entire nation, toward the historic Civil Rights Act of 1964 and the Voting Rights Act of 1965. Drawing on a wealth of newly available sources -- Johnson's taped telephone conversations, voluminous FBI wiretap logs, previously secret communications between the FBI and the president -- Nick Kotz gives us a dramatic narrative, rich in dialogue, that presents this momentous period with thrilling immediacy. Judgment Days offers needed perspective on a presidency too often linked solely to the tragedy of Vietnam. We watch Johnson applying the arm-twisting tactics that made him a legend in the Senate, and we follow King as he keeps the pressure on in the South through protest and passive resistance.","publicationYear":2005,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"African Americans","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-judgment-days-lyndon-baines-johnson-martin-luther-king-jr-and-the-laws-that-changed-america-nick"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Civil rights","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-judgment-days-lyndon-baines-johnson-martin-luther-king-jr-and-the-laws-that-changed-america-nick"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Friends and associates","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-judgment-days-lyndon-baines-johnson-martin-luther-king-jr-and-the-laws-that-changed-america-nick"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"History","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-judgment-days-lyndon-baines-johnson-martin-luther-king-jr-and-the-laws-that-changed-america-nick"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Legal status, laws","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-judgment-days-lyndon-baines-johnson-martin-luther-king-jr-and-the-laws-that-changed-america-nick"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Political aspects","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-judgment-days-lyndon-baines-johnson-martin-luther-king-jr-and-the-laws-that-changed-america-nick"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Politics and government","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-judgment-days-lyndon-baines-johnson-martin-luther-king-jr-and-the-laws-that-changed-america-nick"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Race relations","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-judgment-days-lyndon-baines-johnson-martin-luther-king-jr-and-the-laws-that-changed-america-nick"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Relations with African Americans","sourceId":"source-ope